# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything below identifies your actual home network. Publishing a gateway MAC
# or SSID is enough to locate your home address via public wardriving
# databases (WiGLE, and the location services baked into every phone OS).
#
# Screenshots and sample data for the README and the write-up come from the
# synthetic seed generator (`pnma seed`), never from a live database.
# See THREAT_MODEL.md, "Publishing risk".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config/pnma.toml
config/*.local.toml
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, `data/` also matches
# `pnma/data/`, which is where `pnma oui-update` writes the vendored IEEE
# table -- the one file in a directory called data that is meant to ship.
# Stray databases anywhere are still caught by the *.db rules below.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.pcap
*.pcapng
logs/
*.log

# Secrets never belong in the repo. Webhook URLs go in the OS credential store.
.env
.env.*
secrets.toml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host forensics output. Contains this machine's hostname, LAN address,
# installed software versions, and copies of whatever was investigated --
# the host-data equivalent of a live capture. Same rule applies: it never
# reaches the public repo. Figures for the write-up come from the seed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kms-evidence/
host-evidence/
*.evtx

# Session working screenshots from the SOC-rework audit (not project assets).
Claude outputs/
# Local KEV feed cache (regenerated by `pnma vulns --refresh`).
kev-cache.json
data/quarantine/

# Third-party Claude Code skills installed locally (npx skills add ...)
.claude/skills/
